WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.078 --> 00:00:19.029
Mary Jane was so sweet that I didn't want to tell her I had put the money in

2
00:00:19.069 --> 00:00:20.029
her uncle's coffin.

3
00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:23.572
So I said to her, "I'll write it on a piece of paper.

4
00:00:24.894 --> 00:00:26.355
After I leave town, you can read it.

5
00:00:27.176 --> 00:00:28.136
Then you'll know where to look."

6
00:00:29.638 --> 00:00:34.629
Mary Jane gave me some paper and I scribbled: "I was behind the door and I saw you

7
00:00:34.709 --> 00:00:37.371
crying. I felt very sorry for you.

8
00:00:38.312 --> 00:00:39.232
I put it in the coffin."

9
00:00:40.773 --> 00:00:43.075
Then I folded up the paper and gave it to her.

10
00:00:44.035 --> 00:00:47.898
I didn't think it would be safe for me and Jim to travel on the river in daylight.

11
00:00:48.978 --> 00:00:51.140
I wanted to wait until dark to get away.

12
00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:56.403
But Mary Jane was such an honest person that I knew she would not be able to hide

13
00:00:56.443 --> 00:00:57.484
her feelings all day.

14
00:00:58.568 --> 00:01:02.691
The expression on her face would tell the king and the duke that she knew the truth.

15
00:01:04.092 --> 00:01:07.254
I asked Mary Jane if she could leave the house until evening.

16
00:01:08.075 --> 00:01:10.576
She agreed to visit her friend Hannah Proctor.

17
00:01:11.717 --> 00:01:14.359
She left quickly before the king and the duke woke up.

18
00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:21.384
At breakfast, I told everyone that Hannah Proctor had the mumps and explained that Mary Jane had gone

19
00:01:21.424 --> 00:01:22.124
to look after her.

20
00:01:23.886 --> 00:01:26.868
In the afternoon, I watched the auction in the town square.

21
00:01:28.028 --> 00:01:32.609
By late in the day, almost everything belonging to Peter Wilks had been sold.

22
00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:36.510
But I knew that no money would be paid on the day of the auction.

23
00:01:37.731 --> 00:01:41.112
The duke and the king would have to stay for another day to collect it.

24
00:01:42.032 --> 00:01:44.713
Before that could happen, Mary Jane would come back.

25
00:01:46.253 --> 00:01:49.554
She would tell the truth, and the two scoundrels would be arrested.

26
00:01:50.594 --> 00:01:53.615
By then, I would be safe on the river again with Jim.

27
00:01:54.696 --> 00:01:58.757
I was quite proud of myself and thought I had arranged things very well.

28
00:01:59.758 --> 00:02:02.919
Then I heard loud voices coming toward the center of town.

29
00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:10.083
I turned and saw a well-dressed older gentleman and a nice-looking younger one with his right arm in

30
00:02:10.123 --> 00:02:10.504
a sling.

31
00:02:11.544 --> 00:02:17.187
Some townspeople were with them, and one of them called out, "Here are two more men who say

32
00:02:17.227 --> 00:02:19.548
they are Harvey Wilks and his brother William!"

33
00:02:21.009 --> 00:02:27.080
Wouldn't you think that the king and the duke would give up when they saw the real Englishmen?

34
00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:27.940
Well, they didn't!

35
00:02:28.401 --> 00:02:33.783
The king said in an angry voice, "These men are liars trying to steal our property.

36
00:02:34.784 --> 00:02:35.944
Don't listen to them!"

37
00:02:37.965 --> 00:02:44.348
I could see that some townspeople believed the king, but Doctor Robinson and some others looked pleased to

38
00:02:44.428 --> 00:02:45.288
see the newcomers.

39
00:02:46.369 --> 00:02:49.570
They had never believed that the duke and the king were honest men.

40
00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:53.732
The two new arrivals were very confused by the uproar.

41
00:02:54.804 --> 00:03:00.206
Harvey Wilks, the older gentleman, told their story: They had come all the way from England to see

42
00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:04.707
their dying brother, but they had been delayed when poor William broke his arm.

43
00:03:06.107 --> 00:03:08.848
The king demanded to see written proof of who they were.

44
00:03:09.888 --> 00:03:14.469
Harvey replied that this was impossible because their bags had been lost on the journey.

45
00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:20.211
So it went on for a while with both pairs of men claiming they were the true relatives.

46
00:03:21.311 --> 00:03:24.720
I knew the truth, but if I told it, I'd be in trouble too.

47
00:03:26.141 --> 00:03:28.842
Then I wouldn’t be able to get away and help Jim.

48
00:03:29.802 --> 00:03:35.343
Finally, Harvey Wilks said that Peter, his brother, had a small tattoo on his chest.

49
00:03:36.284 --> 00:03:38.044
He challenged the king to describe it.

50
00:03:39.005 --> 00:03:44.566
"Why, yes," said the king, "he has a small lightning bolt on his chest."

51
00:03:44.586 --> 00:03:47.647
"No," said the old gentleman.

52
00:03:48.247 --> 00:03:50.748
"It is his initials: P and W."

53
00:03:52.108 --> 00:03:57.590
By now, most of the townspeople were so confused that they did not know what to believe.

54
00:03:58.671 --> 00:04:02.493
Doctor Robinson jumped up onto the table that had been used for the auction.

55
00:04:02.513 --> 00:04:05.974
"There's only one way to settle this," he shouted.

56
00:04:05.994 --> 00:04:09.416
"Let's all go to the cemetery and dig up the corpse.

57
00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:13.097
Grab the four men and the boy and make them come with us."

58
00:04:14.638 --> 00:04:19.360
I was very scared, but a townsman was holding me so hard that I couldn't escape.

59
00:04:20.352 --> 00:04:25.175
"If we don't find the tattoo those two scoundrels described, we'll hang you along with them!"

60
00:04:25.756 --> 00:04:26.516
he growled at me.

61
00:04:28.478 --> 00:04:32.661
It was dark and windy in the cemetery, and lightning flashed in the sky.

62
00:04:33.701 --> 00:04:37.484
So many men were helping that it did not take long to dig up the grave.

63
00:04:38.484 --> 00:04:40.926
Then they pulled out the coffin and opened the lid.

64
00:04:41.927 --> 00:04:47.991
A huge lightning bolt lit up the night, and someone yelled, "Look at that—there's a big bag of

65
00:04:48.071 --> 00:04:49.232
gold on his chest!"

66
00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:54.121
Everyone became so excited that they rushed toward the coffin.

67
00:04:54.922 --> 00:05:00.304
The townsman forgot to hold my wrist, and I ran away at once, down the road as fast

68
00:05:00.344 --> 00:05:00.844
as I could.

69
00:05:01.765 --> 00:05:04.126
I ran right through town without seeing anyone.

70
00:05:05.006 --> 00:05:09.428
When I got to the riverbank, a lightning flash showed me a canoe that was pulled up on

71
00:05:09.488 --> 00:05:15.330
shore. I jumped in and paddled until I came to the raft where Jim was waiting.

72
00:05:16.231 --> 00:05:19.232
I had never been so glad to see anyone in my whole life.

73
00:05:20.184 --> 00:05:21.985
"Cut the rope loose and let's go, Jim!"

74
00:05:22.745 --> 00:05:24.185
I yelled, climbing aboard.

75
00:05:24.205 --> 00:05:26.846
"We're finally free of those scoundrels."

76
00:05:29.707 --> 00:05:31.947
In seconds, we were out on the river again.

77
00:05:32.928 --> 00:05:36.629
I felt so relieved that I began to jump and dance on the raft.

78
00:05:37.489 --> 00:05:39.930
Then I heard the sound of paddling behind the raft.

79
00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:42.911
The next lightning flash revealed the truth.

80
00:05:43.371 --> 00:05:46.632
It was the duke and the king in a rowboat, catching up with us.
